>     i think it is equal to the %in%

Not exactly. Using %in% ignores the order in which you are
supplying your ids:

   > x <- c(a=1, b=2, c=3)
   > myids <- c("c", "a")
   > x[names(x) %in% myids]  # NOT equivalent to x[myids]
   a c
   1 3
   > x[match(myids, names(x))]  # equivalent to x[myids]
   c a
   3 1

H.

